# Teacher Question Bank — Backend Architecture

## 1. Overview

The Teacher Question Bank extends Prosno.io's existing question generation system into a **collaborative, trust-gated, curriculum-structured question repository**. Teachers can author questions privately, publish them after generating an exam paper, and browse/reuse questions contributed by others — all within the existing Class → Subject → Chapter hierarchy already present in the codebase.

### Core Design Principles
- **Trust-gated publishing** — not every question is immediately public
- **Curriculum-first browsing** — questions live within the existing hierarchy
- **Non-blocking** — duplicates are warned, never blocked; moderation is async
- **Extensible** — marketplace, AI, and premium packs can be layered on without schema breaks

---

## 2. Context: Existing Codebase

The platform is a **Flask + SQLAlchemy** app backed by **PostgreSQL** (Render) or SQLite (dev). Relevant existing models:

| Model | Purpose |
|---|---|
| [User](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#35-73) | Admin/editor users — needs teacher fields added |
| [Class](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#75-91) | Grade/class level |
| [Subject](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#93-112) | Subject per class |
| [Chapter](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#114-133) | Chapter per subject |
| [Question](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#135-178) | MCQ questions |
| [ShortQuestion](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#180-216) | Short answer (SQ) questions |
| [CQQuestion](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#218-283) | Creative questions (CQ) |
| [QuestionSet](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#312-357) | Teacher-saved question sets (linked to Supabase `user_id`) |
| [GeneratedPaper](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#285-310) | Generated exam papers |

> **Key insight**: The existing [Question](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#135-178), [ShortQuestion](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#180-216), and [CQQuestion](file:///d:/Work/Programming/prosno.io/app/models.py#218-283) models are **admin-managed content**. The Question Bank introduces a **teacher-owned variant** of these, with metadata, visibility, and status tracking.

---

## 3. Database Schema

### 3.1 New / Extended Tables

#### `teacher_profiles` (new)
Extends the existing Supabase user system with teacher-specific metadata.

```sql
CREATE TABLE teacher_profiles (
    id              SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    user_id         VARCHAR(100) UNIQUE NOT NULL,  -- Supabase UUID
    display_name    VARCHAR(200),
    is_trusted      BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
    trust_granted_at TIMESTAMP,
    trust_granted_by VARCHAR(100),                 -- admin user_id

    -- Trust thresholds (cached counters for performance)
    approved_questions_count  INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    reputation_score          INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    account_created_at        TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),

    -- Contribution stats (denormalized for performance)
    questions_created    INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    questions_published  INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    questions_used       INTEGER DEFAULT 0,  -- usage_count sum by others
    total_downloads      INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    average_rating       NUMERIC(3,2) DEFAULT 0.00,

    -- Gamification
    contributor_rank     VARCHAR(50) DEFAULT 'Newcomer',
    -- e.g. Newcomer → Contributor → Senior → Expert → Master

    created_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_teacher_profiles_user_id ON teacher_profiles(user_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_teacher_profiles_reputation ON teacher_profiles(reputation_score DESC);
```

---

#### `bank_questions` (new — core table)
The teacher question bank's central table. Separate from the admin-managed `questions` / `short_questions` / `cq_questions` tables, but shares the same Class→Subject→Chapter foreign keys.

```sql
CREATE TABLE bank_questions (
    id              SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    teacher_id      VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,         -- Supabase UUID (creator)

    -- Curriculum location (existing FK hierarchy)
    class_id        INTEGER REFERENCES classes(id),
    subject_id      INTEGER REFERENCES subjects(id),
    chapter_id      INTEGER REFERENCES chapters(id),

    -- Question content
    question_type   VARCHAR(10) NOT NULL,           -- 'MCQ', 'SQ', 'CQ'
    question_text   TEXT NOT NULL,
    answer          TEXT,
    explanation     TEXT,

    -- MCQ-specific
    answer_options  JSONB,                          -- ["A","B","C","D"]
    correct_answer  VARCHAR(500),

    -- CQ-specific
    stem            TEXT,
    part_ka         TEXT,
    part_kha        TEXT,
    part_ga         TEXT,
    part_gha        TEXT,
    marks_ka        SMALLINT,
    marks_kha       SMALLINT,
    marks_ga        SMALLINT,
    marks_gha       SMALLINT,

    -- Classification metadata
    topic           VARCHAR(200),
    difficulty      VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'medium',   -- easy / medium / hard
    marks           SMALLINT DEFAULT 1,
    board           VARCHAR(100),                   -- e.g. Dhaka Board
    year            SMALLINT,

    -- Publishing state
    visibility      VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'private',  -- private / pending / public / rejected
    status          VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'draft',    -- draft / submitted / approved / rejected
    published_at    TIMESTAMP,
    rejected_at     TIMESTAMP,
    rejection_reason TEXT,

    -- Source tracking
    origin          VARCHAR(20) DEFAULT 'manual',   -- manual / ai_generated / copied
    source_question_id INTEGER REFERENCES bank_questions(id),  -- if copied

    -- Usage & quality metrics
    usage_count     INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    download_count  INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    rating_total    INTEGER DEFAULT 0,
    rating_count    INTEGER DEFAULT 0,

    -- Similarity fingerprint for duplicate detection
    text_hash       VARCHAR(64),                    -- SHA256 of normalized question_text
    embedding_vector VECTOR(768),                   -- pgvector for semantic similarity (future)

    created_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
    updated_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_bq_teacher_id   ON bank_questions(teacher_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_chapter_id   ON bank_questions(chapter_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_subject_id   ON bank_questions(subject_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_class_id     ON bank_questions(class_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_visibility   ON bank_questions(visibility);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_question_type ON bank_questions(question_type);
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_text_hash    ON bank_questions(text_hash);
-- Composite for curriculum browsing
CREATE INDEX idx_bq_browse ON bank_questions(class_id, subject_id, chapter_id, question_type, visibility);
```

---

#### `moderation_queue` (new)
Tracks questions awaiting admin review before becoming public.

```sql
CREATE TABLE moderation_queue (
    id              SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    question_id     INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES bank_questions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    submitted_by    VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,           -- teacher user_id
    submitted_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
    reviewed_by     VARCHAR(100),                    -- admin user_id
    reviewed_at     TIMESTAMP,
    decision        VARCHAR(20),                     -- approved / rejected
    admin_notes     TEXT,
    priority        SMALLINT DEFAULT 5              -- 1=high, 10=low
);

CREATE INDEX idx_mq_decision ON moderation_queue(decision) WHERE decision IS NULL;
CREATE INDEX idx_mq_submitted_at ON moderation_queue(submitted_at);
```

---

#### `question_interactions` (new)
Tracks per-teacher actions on bank questions: usage, saves, ratings.

```sql
CREATE TABLE question_interactions (
    id              SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    question_id     INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES bank_questions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    teacher_id      VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    action_type     VARCHAR(20) NOT NULL,            -- 'used' / 'saved' / 'copied' / 'rated'
    rating_value    SMALLINT CHECK (rating_value BETWEEN 1 AND 5),
    question_set_id INTEGER REFERENCES question_sets(id),   -- if used in a question set
    paper_id        INTEGER REFERENCES generated_papers(id), -- if used in a paper
    created_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),

    UNIQUE (question_id, teacher_id, action_type)   -- one rating per teacher per question
);

CREATE INDEX idx_qi_question_id ON question_interactions(question_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_qi_teacher_id  ON question_interactions(teacher_id);
```

---

#### `teacher_library` (new)
Questions a teacher has saved to their personal library.

```sql
CREATE TABLE teacher_library (
    id          SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    teacher_id  VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    question_id INTEGER NOT NULL REFERENCES bank_questions(id) ON DELETE CASCADE,
    saved_at    TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),
    notes       TEXT,

    UNIQUE (teacher_id, question_id)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_tl_teacher_id ON teacher_library(teacher_id);
```

---

#### `teacher_badges` (new)
Gamification — awarded badges per teacher.

```sql
CREATE TABLE teacher_badges (
    id          SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    teacher_id  VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    badge_slug  VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL,               -- e.g. 'top_contributor', 'math_specialist'
    badge_name  VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    awarded_at  TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW(),

    UNIQUE (teacher_id, badge_slug)
);

CREATE INDEX idx_tb_teacher_id ON teacher_badges(teacher_id);
```

---

#### `publish_prompts` (new)
Tracks prompt state shown to teachers after generating an exam paper — whether they've responded and what they chose.

```sql
CREATE TABLE publish_prompts (
    id              SERIAL PRIMARY KEY,
    teacher_id      VARCHAR(100) NOT NULL,
    paper_id        INTEGER REFERENCES generated_papers(id),
    question_set_id INTEGER REFERENCES question_sets(id),
    question_ids    JSONB NOT NULL,                  -- [bank_question_id, ...]
    responded       BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE,
    decision        VARCHAR(20),                     -- 'publish' / 'keep_private'
    responded_at    TIMESTAMP,
    created_at      TIMESTAMP DEFAULT NOW()
);

CREATE INDEX idx_pp_teacher_id ON publish_prompts(teacher_id);
CREATE INDEX idx_pp_responded  ON publish_prompts(responded) WHERE responded = FALSE;
```

---

### 3.2 Schema Relationships Diagram

```
classes
  └── subjects
        └── chapters
              └── bank_questions ◄── moderation_queue
                    │                      │
                    ├── question_interactions    (ratings, usage tracking)
                    ├── teacher_library          (saved questions)
                    └── publish_prompts          (post-paper prompt state)

teacher_profiles ──► bank_questions (teacher_id)
teacher_profiles ◄── teacher_badges
```

---

## 4. Trust & Publishing Workflow

### 4.1 Trust Resolution

A teacher is considered **trusted** when any of the following are met (evaluated on publish attempt):

```python
def is_teacher_trusted(profile: TeacherProfile) -> bool:
    if profile.is_trusted:          # manually granted by admin
        return True
    days_old = (now() - profile.account_created_at).days
    return (
        profile.approved_questions_count >= 50
        and days_old >= 30
        and profile.reputation_score >= 100
    )
```

Trust thresholds are configurable (stored in a `system_config` key-value table or environment variable).

---

### 4.2 Publishing State Machine

```
       Teacher creates questions (bank_questions.visibility = 'private')
                          │
              Teacher generates exam paper
                          │
                  System fires publish_prompt
                          │
              ┌───────────┴──────────┐
         [Publish]            [Keep Private]
              │                    │
    is_trusted = TRUE?        stays 'private'
        │            │
       YES           NO
        │            │
   visibility     visibility  →  moderation_queue
   = 'public'     = 'pending'          │
   status         status              ADMIN REVIEWS
   = 'approved'   = 'submitted'        │
                                ┌─────┴─────┐
                           [Approve]   [Reject]
                                │           │
                           'public'    'rejected'
                           'approved'  rejection_reason
```

---

### 4.3 Publish API Flow (Sequence)

```
1. POST /api/v1/bank/papers/{paper_id}/publish-prompt
   → Creates publish_prompt record, returns list of questions to potentially publish

2. POST /api/v1/bank/publish-prompt/{prompt_id}/respond
   Body: { decision: "publish" | "keep_private", question_ids: [...] }
   → For each selected question:
       a. Check duplicate (text_hash match or semantic similarity)
       b. If duplicate: return warning with existing_question_id
       c. If no duplicate OR teacher confirms:
           - trusted teacher → set visibility='public', status='approved'
           - new teacher     → set visibility='pending', insert moderation_queue row
   → Update publish_prompt.responded = true

3. Async (background job):
   → Update teacher_profiles counters
   → Check badge eligibility
   → Notify teacher of moderation decision (when reviewed)
```

---

## 5. API Design

All endpoints are REST, returning JSON. Auth is via Supabase JWT (`Authorization: Bearer <token>`).

### 5.1 Teacher Profile

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/profile` | Get own teacher profile + stats |
| `PUT` | `/api/v1/bank/profile` | Update display name, etc. |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/teachers/{user_id}/profile` | View another teacher's public profile |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/leaderboard` | Top contributors (paginated) |

### 5.2 Question Authoring

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/questions` | Create a new question (private by default) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/questions` | List own questions (with filters) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}` | Get a specific question |
| `PUT` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}` | Edit a question (only if private/rejected) |
| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}` | Soft-delete (only own private questions) |

**POST body example:**
```json
{
  "class_id": 3,
  "subject_id": 12,
  "chapter_id": 45,
  "question_type": "MCQ",
  "question_text": "গতিশক্তির সূত্র কী?",
  "answer_options": ["Ek = ½mv²", "Ek = mv", "Ek = mgh", "Ek = ma"],
  "correct_answer": "Ek = ½mv²",
  "explanation": "গতিশক্তি হলো...",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "marks": 1,
  "topic": "গতি ও শক্তি"
}
```

### 5.3 Question Bank Browsing

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/browse` | Browse by class/subject/chapter/type |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/browse/classes` | List all classes with question counts |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/browse/classes/{id}/subjects` | Subjects with question counts |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/browse/subjects/{id}/chapters` | Chapters with question counts |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/browse/chapters/{id}/questions` | Questions in a chapter (grouped by type) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/search` | Full-text search across public questions |

**Browse query parameters:**
```
?class_id=3
&subject_id=12
&chapter_id=45
&question_type=MCQ        # MCQ | SQ | CQ
&difficulty=medium
&sort=rating | usage | newest
&page=1&per_page=20
```

**Browse response shape:**
```json
{
  "chapter": { "id": 45, "name": "Motion" },
  "grouped": {
    "MCQ": [ { ...question }, ... ],
    "SQ":  [ ... ],
    "CQ":  [ ... ]
  },
  "counts": { "MCQ": 120, "SQ": 45, "CQ": 30 }
}
```

### 5.4 Question Interactions

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/use` | Add question to own question set |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/save` | Save to personal library |
| `DELETE` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/save` | Remove from library |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/rate` | Rate a question (1–5 stars) |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/copy` | Copy & edit (creates private draft) |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/library` | Get own saved library |

### 5.5 Publishing Workflow

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/papers/{paper_id}/publish-prompt` | Trigger post-paper prompt |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/publish-prompt/{id}` | Get prompt details |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/bank/publish-prompt/{id}/respond` | Submit publish/keep-private decision |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/bank/questions/{id}/duplicate-check` | Check for duplicates before publishing |

### 5.6 Moderation (Admin)

| Method | Path | Description |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/v1/admin/moderation/queue` | List pending questions |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/admin/moderation/{queue_id}` | View a specific item |
| `POST` | `/api/v1/admin/moderation/{queue_id}/decide` | Approve or reject |
| `PATCH` | `/api/v1/admin/teachers/{user_id}/trust` | Manually grant/revoke trusted status |
| `GET` | `/api/v1/admin/teachers` | List all teacher profiles |

